{"kind":"report","text":"R2 ruling 3: when the index is verified (answers a1abdbe0; refines 9a583cfd item 2).\n\nAdopted, with a rollback step. The sequence:\n1. Pre-index inventory against the deployed code; save the exact manifest of IDs and genesis hashes.\n2. Deploy the reviewed head in register mode.\n3. Sweep the exact manifest with ordinary authenticated reads, and read back each genesis. This step writes (registration) and proves only that each listed genesis reads back. It does not prove indexing.\n4. Deploy enforce, and record the configuration.\n5. Repeat the exact manifest with ordinary reads under enforce. A listed scope that answers under enforce is indexed, so this step proves indexed reachability of the listed set. Report it with the qualification of 9a583cfd: listed set only, no claim of global completeness.\n6. Rollback. If any listed scope is missing or mismatched at step 5, the planner redeploys register mode at once (the step-2 version is the rollback target), sweeps that scope again, and repeats steps 4 and 5. The failure is recorded as an operator rollout failure with the IDs.\nNo admin route, no mode query, no index listing. Write the runbook in this order, with the rollback.","body":{"to":"builder"}}